  "release": 245,
  "title": "Scroll back",
  "since": "2026-11-12",
  "confirmed_by": null,
  "owner_words": null,
  "deployed_build": 244,
  "note": "Packaged 12 Nov 2026, the same hour as the regression it repairs. The owner installed v244 and: 'i cant even scroll anything on mobile now, everything has just stopped'. The cause was NOT the blur or the layers — it was content-visibility. A content-visibility:auto subtree is not laid out until it is near the viewport: it reports the placeholder height from contain-intrinsic-size instead of its real height, and the lazy images inside it never start. It had been sprinkled across the app over several releases (.p-grid, .pillars, .ugc-wall, .catbar-outer, .p-card, .ds-card, #view > section, the footer) and v244 added two more. On a phone that is a document shorter than its content — the page stops scrolling part way — and blank cards that never wake. v245 deletes every content-visibility and contain-intrinsic-size declaration from the bundle, forbids them with a universal guard, removes the html/body overflow-x:hidden v244 added, makes the decoration parking impossible to stick (400ms watchdog + hashchange/pageshow/visibility), wakes any blank picture in front of the shopper, and adds ?nofx=1 as a kill switch. The v244 blur work (opaque sticky bars, hover-only card layers) is kept — that part is sound. Contains v237-v244.",
  "zip": "shivaa-update-v245.zip",
  "sha256": "68c2e0b3d9b951aab4d96fcd3a031f0e0d5e0dcc0dea5de861aba7d0386c8552"
 },
